# Files currently over the size limit, frozen at their present length.
#
# Scope is verify_code_size.py's, not "shell": linux/scripts, linux/host-config,
# docs/scripts and linux/llm-stack by *.sh/*.py, plus the Dockerfile* at the top of
# linux/. Seven of the rows below are llm-stack, in scope since EX1 (2026-09-07).
#
# Format: <path> | <lines> | <reason>
#
# Same four-way contract as function-size.allow: growth, a new offender, an
# unrecorded shrink and a stale entry all fail. Shrinking a file means updating
# its number here; deleting the line once it drops under the limit.
#
# The refactor entries live in docs/refactoring-backlog.md F2.

# --- EX1 2026-09-07: linux/llm-stack enters the scan set. These 47 rows are the
# territory the extent gates could never see; every one was read and given a
# verdict in the same wave that widened SCAN, so none is a bare baseline. 34 of
# them say DEBT and name their seam -- that is the honest state of a benchmark
# harness nobody had reviewed for shape. docs/refactoring-backlog.md EX1
linux/Dockerfile.media | 910 | Adjacent core copies share their unchanged pre-RUN closure; the standalone logger is carried for partial media rebuilds. Previous review: 911 -> 912 on 2026-10-18: the ORT GPU RUN mounts linux/scripts/patches/onnxruntime again, for the CUDA cstdint patch. PRIOR: 908 -> 911 on 2026-10-17: the hub sccache build -- ENABLE_SCCACHE_RUST/CUDA default 1, and ENABLE_SCCACHE_HIP, its own switch, as an ARG and in the ENV block. PRIOR: 879 -> 908 on 2026-10-17: the shared S3 level -- each of the 14 sccache RUNs gains `--mount=type=secret,id=sccache_s3,required=false` and a closing `bash /opt/scripts/core/sccache-s3-level.sh drain`, and the Arm NN RUN, which mounts no 01-core, the library bind. PRIOR: 880 -> 879 on 2026-10-13: CON95 -- the ORT GPU RUN loses the linux/scripts/patches/onnxruntime mount, since v1.31.0 carries upstream's GCC 16 epilogue fix and the patch is gone. PRIOR: 877 -> 880 on 2026-10-13: the shared wasm cache is stamped only once it holds a *.wasm (a non-amd64 target skips the wasm step with rc 0), an elif arm and its one-line why. PRIOR: 873 -> 877 on 2026-10-09: CON75/CON79 1b -- FT_TORCH_TWIN as an ARG in the app-wheelhouse stage (exported to build-app-wheelhouse.sh) and in the final stage, whose free-threaded-store.sh expects the riscv64 torch twin while it is 1, each behind a one-line why. PRIOR: 870 -> 873 on 2026-10-08: CON79 -- the pyav RUN bind-mounts the chain ORT and puts its lib on LD_LIBRARY_PATH behind a one-line why, so the cp314t proof can load libavfilter. PRIOR: 864 -> 870 on 2026-10-07: CON79 4 -- the one twin table both lanes read (03-media/free-threaded-twins.txt) is bind-mounted per file beside free-threaded-wheels.sh into the same six twin RUNs, one line each. PRIOR: 842 -> 864 on 2026-10-07: the cp314t twins -- the free-threaded library and helper bind-mounted per file into the six RUNs that build or store a twin, the uv cache on the ORT cpu and TVM RUNs, the three twin COPYs into final, and its --free-threaded repair, verify and store steps. PRIOR: 841 -> 842 on 2026-10-02: CON42 -- the GCC-16 epilogue-scalars patch bind-mounted per file (linux/scripts/patches/onnxruntime) into the cpu-verify RUN. PRIOR: 814 -> 841 on 2026-10-01: CON42 -- the gated deepstream stage (FROM gstreamer, one RUN, empty unless ENABLE_DEEPSTREAM=true) and its ccache/sccache mounts, and its COPY at the end of final. PRIOR: 1248 -> 814 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: 1246 -> 1248 on 2026-09-23: the chain-wheel manifest follow step of the ORT census. PRIOR: 1241 -> 1246 on 2026-09-23: G2 (03-media/ort-provenance.sh, the shared ORT build gate) is mounted per file into its five consumer RUNs (opencv x2, ffmpeg, gstreamer, the genai verify RUN), one line each. PRIOR: 1236 -> 1241 on 2026-09-23: the genai verify RUN mounts and runs verify-genai-ort.sh (GenAI's chain-ORT proof) behind a 2-line why. PRIOR: 1162 -> 1175 on 2026-09-10: TWO sessions fixed the same bug the same day and the merge keeps both halves -- their measured failure story (a native arm64 host resolved every unqualified name to :amd64, binutils:amd64 replaced the aarch64 assembler and `as -EL` failed) with their build_arch_oci fallback, routed through AS1's ubuntu_arch_uses_ports table so the host and target stanzas cannot answer 'which archive' differently. Neither side's count survived (1174 vs 1170); 1175 is measured.
linux/scripts/06-packaging/smoke-runtime-image.sh | 2469 | Re-measured 2745 -> 2481 after moving consumer fact collection, row dispatch and shared verdicts into runtime-consumer-contract.sh and consolidating optional smoke runner paths; browser and emulator checks remain with smoke-specific assertions. Re-measured after sharing GStreamer/libunwind probe completion, functional runtime reporting, shipped-truth section setup, verdict-row accounting and pinned-version probe handling.
